{"path":"ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-spec-structure.xml#MODULE_SPEC_MARKDOWN_STRUCTURE","detail":"Instruction says 'this module spec's own acronym' but not how it is derived. I authored NORM-REQ-1/2; sdd-check reported SDD_REQ_ACRONYM_MISMATCH requiring NOR (call_00_X2XWiLShvlTbFWqwmRNy0009). This forced a second full-file Write (call_00_JFeTuQEgwAcey8MkHmFJ6968)."},
{"path":"ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-spec-structure.xml#MODULE_DECISION_LOG","detail":"References DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT without a local definition; it lives in infra.directive.xml, which I located only via grep (call_00_mCFh8uQPZwubMgvnLbET1946) and sed (call_00_ET_6GiCwsAC9Cdx57uLCFgR5777). A direct pointer would remove that search."},
{"path":"ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/module-spec-structure.xml#IMPLEMENTATION_INSIGHTS","detail":"Unclear whether the optional appendix should be omitted entirely or retained with an N/A statement. I chose retained-with-N/A; the checker did not adjudicate that choice."},
{"path":"ai/directives/sdd-v2/module.directive.xml#STEP_6_HANDOFF","detail":"Requires noting deviations but does not state how to phrase pending operator handoff in a module spec. I inferred it from the seeded scope spec and brief; not mechanically confirmed."},
{"path":"trace:call_00_Cv9ylWa0PyKe6gaU8sQd4159","detail":"Directory listing after the DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT location was already found added no new decision-relevant fact; could be avoided."}
],"uncertainties":[
"Preferred test framework for a TypeScript module was not specified; node-test was a conservative default, unverified against any seeded stack directive.",
"Whether Implementation Insights must be absent rather than N/A when no implementation occurred is unknown; no check complained.",
"Whether the single-entity 'no ER sketch' note satisfies the inventory format is assumed from its wording, not tool-verified.",
"Whether the consumer-only dependency mermaid satisfies the graph-shape expectation or should instead be omitted as no real edge exists is unknown; sdd-check passed it."
],"nextHypothesis":"Document the requirement-acronym derivation rule (filename stem, uppercased prefix as used by sdd-check) directly in the MODULE_REQUIREMENTS comment of module-spec-structure.xml, and add a direct pointer to DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT's owning file. Test whether this removes the acronym warning and the resulting second whole-file write without weakening the check."}
